moving, even when it doesn't feel like

288
00:09:11,728 --> 00:09:11,912
it.

289
00:09:12,262 --> 00:09:13,544
Stage five trap:

290
00:09:13,544 --> 00:09:15,547
market drops feel bigger.

291
00:09:15,727 --> 00:09:17,962
At sixty thousand dollars invested,

292
00:09:17,962 --> 00:09:20,389
a twenty percent market drop is twelve

293
00:09:20,389 --> 00:09:21,474
thousand dollars.

294
00:09:21,654 --> 00:09:23,333
That might be more than you saved

295
00:09:23,333 --> 00:09:23,790
all year.

296
00:09:23,970 --> 00:09:25,116
For the first time,

297
00:09:25,116 --> 00:09:26,624
a bad year can wipe out a

298
00:09:26,624 --> 00:09:27,529
year of effort,

299
00:09:27,529 --> 00:09:28,614
at least on paper.

300
00:09:28,794 --> 00:09:31,337
This is when panic selling becomes tempting.

301
00:09:31,687 --> 00:09:33,635
The fix: write a note to your

302
00:09:33,635 --> 00:09:34,710
future self now,

303
00:09:34,710 --> 00:09:35,785
before the drop.

304
00:09:35,965 --> 00:09:38,478
When my portfolio falls twenty percent,

305
00:09:38,478 --> 00:09:40,540
I will keep investing and I will

306
00:09:40,540 --> 00:09:41,120
not sell.

307
00:09:41,300 --> 00:09:42,345
And check your mix.

308
00:09:42,525 --> 00:09:44,230
If drops truly keep you up at

309
00:09:44,230 --> 00:09:46,818
night, a slightly more conservative mix that

310
00:09:46,818 --> 00:09:48,759
you can stick with is better than

311
00:09:48,759 --> 00:09:50,524
an aggressive one you abandon.

312
00:09:50,874 --> 00:09:52,097
Stage six trap:

313
00:09:52,097 --> 00:09:54,055
the finish line feeling.

314
00:09:54,235 --> 00:09:56,603
You're close, and it's tempting to ease

315
00:09:56,603 --> 00:09:57,878
off, reward yourself,

316
00:09:57,878 --> 00:10:00,247
or start spending ahead of reaching the

317
00:10:00,247 --> 00:10:00,550
goal.

318
00:10:00,730 --> 00:10:01,795
Or the opposite,

319
00:10:01,795 --> 00:10:04,457
taking bigger risks to get there faster.

320
00:10:04,637 --> 00:10:06,472
Both can delay you by years.

321
00:10:06,821 --> 00:10:08,932
The fix: keep the exact same habits

322
00:10:08,932 --> 00:10:10,258
for the final stretch.

323
00:10:10,438 --> 00:10:12,528
Remember, at this stage your money is

324
00:10:12,528 --> 00:10:14,223
doing a big share of the work.

325
00:10:14,403 --> 00:10:16,360
Don't change the system that got you

326
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:16,632
here.

327
00:10:16,812 --> 00:10:19,352
And plan your celebration in advance,

328
00:10:19,352 --> 00:10:20,244
a modest one,

329
00:10:20,244 --> 00:10:22,646
so it doesn't turn into a lifestyle

330
00:10:22,646 --> 00:10:23,058
reset.

331
00:10:23,408 --> 00:10:24,395
Quick pause.

332
00:10:24,575 --> 00:10:26,658
If you're on this journey right now,

333
00:10:26,658 --> 00:10:28,105
subscribe to the channel.

334
00:10:28,285 --> 00:10:30,071
It's free, and I'll be here with

335
00:10:30,071 --> 00:10:31,187
you for every stage.

336
00:10:31,367 --> 00:10:32,575
Now, the playbook.

337
00:10:32,755 --> 00:10:35,495
Exactly what to do at each stage.

338
00:10:35,844 --> 00:10:36,738
Angle three.

339
00:10:36,918 --> 00:10:37,661
The playbook.

340
00:10:37,841 --> 00:10:40,390
Six stages, with the exact moves for

341
00:10:40,390 --> 00:10:40,744
each.

342
00:10:41,093 --> 00:10:42,814
If you want the whole plan in

343
00:10:42,814 --> 00:10:44,298
one sentence, here it is.

344
00:10:44,478 --> 00:10:46,036
Build a small cushion,

345
00:10:46,036 --> 00:10:47,028
get the match,

346
00:10:47,028 --> 00:10:48,727
kill high interest debt,

347
00:10:48,727 --> 00:10:50,711
build a real emergency fund,

348
00:10:50,711 --> 00:10:53,969
invest ten to fifteen percent automatically in

349
00:10:53,969 --> 00:10:55,031
low cost funds,

350
00:10:55,031 --> 00:10:56,235
grow your income,

351
00:10:56,235 --> 00:10:57,864
and don't interrupt it.

352
00:10:58,044 --> 00:10:59,855
Everything else is detail.

353
00:11:00,035 --> 00:11:02,334
Now let's go stage by stage.

354
00:11:02,684 --> 00:11:05,877
Stage one, zero to one thousand dollars.

355
00:11:06,057 --> 00:11:08,080
The goal is a starter cushion that

356
00:11:08,080 --> 00:11:10,578
breaks the loop of every surprise becoming

357
00:11:10,578 --> 00:11:10,875
debt.

358
00:11:11,055 --> 00:11:13,540
Open a separate high yield savings account,

359
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:15,678
ideally at a different bank from your

360
00:11:15,678 --> 00:11:17,932
checking, so the money isn't staring at

361
00:11:17,932 --> 00:11:18,741
you every day.

362
00:11:19,091 --> 00:11:21,490
Set an automatic transfer on payday,

363
00:11:21,490 --> 00:11:23,155
even twenty five dollars.

364
00:11:23,335 --> 00:11:25,748
Cancel two subscriptions you don't use,

365
00:11:25,748 --> 00:11:27,665
and send that money to savings.

366
00:11:27,845 --> 00:11:29,819
Sell a few things you don't need.

367
00:11:29,999 --> 00:11:31,510
And put any windfall,

368
00:11:31,510 --> 00:11:32,805
like a tax refund,

369
00:11:32,805 --> 00:11:33,668
straight in.

370
00:11:33,848 --> 00:11:36,240
Most people can finish this stage in

371
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:37,435
two to six months.

372
00:11:37,785 --> 00:11:39,827
The common mistake in stage one is

373
00:11:39,827 --> 00:11:42,650
waiting for the perfect budget before starting.

374
00:11:42,830 --> 00:11:43,631
You don't need one.

375
00:11:43,811 --> 00:11:45,019
You need a transfer.

376
00:11:45,199 --> 00:11:46,324
A real example:

377
00:11:46,324 --> 00:11:47,824
Kayla, twenty three,

378
00:11:47,824 --> 00:11:50,674
set up a twenty dollar weekly transfer

379
00:11:50,674 --> 00:11:52,850
and sold an old game console.

380
00:11:53,030 --> 00:11:55,286
She hit one thousand dollars in about

381
00:11:55,286 --> 00:11:57,238
four months, and said it was the

382
00:11:57,238 --> 00:11:59,251
first time in her life she didn't

383
00:11:59,251 --> 00:12:01,447
panic when her car needed new tires.

384
00:12:01,797 --> 00:12:04,780
Stage two, one thousand to ten thousand.

385
00:12:04,960 --> 00:12:06,156
Two jobs here.

386
00:12:06,336 --> 00:12:09,006
First, make sure you're getting any employer

387
00:12:09,006 --> 00:12:11,736
retirement match, because that's part of your

388
00:12:11,736 --> 00:12:11,979
pay.

389
00:12:12,159 --> 00:12:14,092
Contribute at least enough to get it,

390
00:12:14,092 --> 00:12:15,502
even while paying off debt.

391
00:12:15,853 --> 00:12:17,954
Second, attack high interest debt.

392
00:12:18,134 --> 00:12:20,208
List every debt by interest rate,

393
00:12:20,208 --> 00:12:22,281
and pay extra on the highest rate

394
00:12:22,281 --> 00:12:24,983
first, while making minimum payments on the

395
00:12:24,983 --> 00:12:25,297
rest.

396
00:12:25,477 --> 00:12:27,648
Once high interest debt is gone,

397
00:12:27,648 --> 00:12:30,158
build your emergency fund to three to

398
00:12:30,158 --> 00:12:32,397
six months of essential expenses.

399
00:12:32,577 --> 00:12:34,852
This stage often takes one to three

400
00:12:34,852 --> 00:12:36,803
years, depending on your debt.

401
00:12:37,153 --> 00:12:38,569
A tip for this stage.

402
00:12:38,749 --> 00:12:40,181
When a debt is paid off,

403
00:12:40,181 --> 00:12:42,987
don't let that payment disappear into spending.

404
00:12:43,167 --> 00:12:44,818
Roll it into the next debt,

405
00:12:44,818 --> 00:12:46,592
then into the emergency fund.

406
00:12:46,772 --> 00:12:48,945
You're already used to living without that

407
00:12:48,945 --> 00:12:49,256
money.

408
00:12:49,436 --> 00:12:50,295
Keep it working.

409
00:12:50,646 --> 00:12:52,935
The common mistake in stage two is

410
00:12:52,935 --> 00:12:55,225
skipping the match to pay off debt

411
00:12:55,225 --> 00:12:55,696
faster.

412
00:12:55,876 --> 00:12:57,551
That's usually a bad trade,

413
00:12:57,551 --> 00:12:59,909
because the match is an instant return

414
00:12:59,909 --> 00:13:01,646
that debt payoff can't beat.

415
00:13:01,826 --> 00:13:04,742
Another mistake is closing every credit card

416
00:13:04,742 --> 00:13:06,133
the moment it's paid.

417
00:13:06,313 --> 00:13:07,912
Sometimes keeping an old,

418
00:13:07,912 --> 00:13:10,086
no fee card open helps your credit

419
00:13:10,086 --> 00:13:10,597
history.

420
00:13:10,777 --> 00:13:12,455
Just don't use it to rebuild a

421
00:13:12,455 --> 00:13:12,902
balance.

422
00:13:13,252 --> 00:13:16,200
Stage three, ten to twenty five thousand.

423
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:18,853
Now investing begins in earnest.

424
00:13:19,033 --> 00:13:20,595
If you haven't already,

425
00:13:20,595 --> 00:13:23,176
open a retirement account like an IRA,

426
00:13:23,176 --> 00:13:26,435
or raise your workplace plan contributions above

427
00:13:26,435 --> 00:13:27,114
the match.

428
00:13:27,294 --> 00:13:29,561
Choose simple, diversified,

429
00:13:29,561 --> 00:13:30,821
low cost funds,

430
00:13:30,821 --> 00:13:33,676
like broad index funds or a target

431
00:13:33,676 --> 00:13:34,515
date fund.

432
00:13:34,866 --> 00:13:36,676
Aim for a savings rate of at

433
00:13:36,676 --> 00:13:39,004
least ten to fifteen percent of your

434
00:13:39,004 --> 00:13:41,785
gross income, including any employer match.

435
00:13:41,965 --> 00:13:43,703
If that feels impossible,

436
00:13:43,703 --> 00:13:45,858
start where you can and add one

437
00:13:45,858 --> 00:13:47,596
percent every few months.

438
00:13:47,776 --> 00:13:50,760
Turn on automatic contribution increases if your

439
00:13:50,760 --> 00:13:51,816
plan offers them.

440
00:13:52,167 --> 00:13:54,547
The common mistake in stage three is

441
00:13:54,547 --> 00:13:55,870
overcomplicating it.

442
00:13:56,050 --> 00:13:58,315
People read about dozens of funds and

443
00:13:58,315 --> 00:14:00,090
strategies and end up frozen.

444
00:14:00,270 --> 00:14:01,353
A single broad,

445
00:14:01,353 --> 00:14:02,364
low cost fund,

446
00:14:02,364 --> 00:14:03,952
or a target date fund,

447
00:14:03,952 --> 00:14:06,911
is a perfectly reasonable starting point.

448
00:14:07,091 --> 00:14:08,670
You can always adjust later.

449
00:14:08,850 --> 00:14:11,676
Another mistake is checking the balance every

450
00:14:11,676 --> 00:14:11,927
day.

451
00:14:12,107 --> 00:14:13,558
Weekly is plenty.

452
00:14:13,738 --> 00:14:14,888
Monthly is better.

453
00:14:15,238 --> 00:14:18,180
Stage four, twenty five to fifty thousand,

454
00:14:18,180 --> 00:14:19,440
the boring middle.

455
00:14:19,620 --> 00:14:21,482
Your main job is to protect the

456
00:14:21,482 --> 00:14:23,103
habit and grow your income.

457
00:14:23,283 --> 00:14:24,665
Apply a raise rule:

458
00:14:24,665 --> 00:14:27,064
at least half of every raise goes

459
00:14:27,064 --> 00:14:28,009
to investing.

460
00:14:28,189 --> 00:14:30,635
Make one career move per year,

461
00:14:30,635 --> 00:14:32,673
a skill, a certification,

462
00:14:32,673 --> 00:14:35,282
a negotiation, or a better role.

463
00:14:35,633 --> 00:14:36,979
Also check your fees.

464
00:14:37,159 --> 00:14:39,563
Find the expense ratio of every fund

465
00:14:39,563 --> 00:14:40,097
you own.

466
00:14:40,277 --> 00:14:42,187
And avoid big new fixed costs,

467
00:14:42,187 --> 00:14:44,033
like a large car payment or a

468
00:14:44,033 --> 00:14:45,434
much bigger apartment,

469
00:14:45,434 --> 00:14:47,471
that would force you to cut your

470
00:14:47,471 --> 00:14:48,299
savings rate.

471
00:14:48,479 --> 00:14:51,241
This stage is mostly about not breaking

472
00:14:51,241 --> 00:14:52,020
what works.

473
00:14:52,371 --> 00:14:54,936
The common mistake in stage four is

474
00:14:54,936 --> 00:14:56,109
the big upgrade.

475
00:14:56,289 --> 00:14:57,923
A new car loan or a much

476
00:14:57,923 --> 00:15:01,056
bigger apartment that quietly cuts the monthly

477
00:15:01,056 --> 00:15:02,349
investment in half.

478
00:15:02,529 --> 00:15:05,132
Another is jumping between strategies,

479
00:15:05,132 --> 00:15:08,008
selling one fund for another after reading

480
00:15:08,008 --> 00:15:09,995
a scary or exciting headline.

481
00:15:10,175 --> 00:15:12,333
Every switch can mean taxes,

482
00:15:12,333 --> 00:15:13,797
fees and lost time.

483
00:15:13,977 --> 00:15:16,334
Boring consistency wins this stage.

484
00:15:16,684 --> 00:15:19,830
Stage five, fifty to seventy five thousand.

485
00:15:20,010 --> 00:15:21,972
Compounding becomes noticeable.

486
00:15:22,152 --> 00:15:23,033
In a good year,

487
00:15:23,033 --> 00:15:25,792
your investments might grow by several thousand

488
00:15:25,792 --> 00:15:26,262
dollars.

489
00:15:26,442 --> 00:15:28,154
This is the stage to get your

490
00:15:28,154 --> 00:15:29,867
financial paperwork in order.

491
00:15:30,047 --> 00:15:32,148
Check the beneficiaries on every account.

492
00:15:32,328 --> 00:15:34,563
If people depend on your income,

493
00:15:34,563 --> 00:15:36,589
consider term life insurance.

494
00:15:36,769 --> 00:15:38,917
And make sure your emergency fund has

495
00:15:38,917 --> 00:15:40,484
kept up with your expenses.

496
00:15:40,835 --> 00:15:42,642
It's also a good time to think

497
00:15:42,642 --> 00:15:43,366
about taxes.

498
00:15:43,546 --> 00:15:46,373
Are you using tax advantaged accounts,

499
00:15:46,373 --> 00:15:47,266
like a 401k,

500
00:15:47,266 --> 00:15:49,871
an IRA, or a health savings account

501
00:15:49,871 --> 00:15:51,285
if you're eligible,

502
00:15:51,285 --> 00:15:52,996
as much as makes sense?

503
00:15:53,176 --> 00:15:55,178
The rules and limits change,

504
00:15:55,178 --> 00:15:57,752
so check the IRS website for current

505
00:15:57,752 --> 00:15:59,039
numbers each year.

506
00:15:59,389 --> 00:16:01,964
The common mistake in stage five is

507
00:16:01,964 --> 00:16:03,951
panic during a market drop.

508
00:16:04,131 --> 00:16:06,978
Someone at sixty thousand watches it fall

509
00:16:06,978 --> 00:16:08,228
to fifty thousand,

510
00:16:08,228 --> 00:16:10,659
sells, and waits for things to feel

511
00:16:10,659 --> 00:16:11,422
safe again.

512
00:16:11,602 --> 00:16:13,212
By the time it feels safe,

513
00:16:13,212 --> 00:16:14,946
prices have often recovered.

514
00:16:15,126 --> 00:16:17,444
Another mistake is taking on too much

515
00:16:17,444 --> 00:16:20,013
risk because the balance feels big enough

516
00:16:20,013 --> 00:16:21,454
to gamble a part of it.

517
00:16:21,804 --> 00:16:24,829
Stage six, seventy five to one hundred

518
00:16:24,829 --> 00:16:26,819
thousand, the final push.

519
00:16:26,999 --> 00:16:28,369
Keep everything the same.

520
00:16:28,549 --> 00:16:30,885
Same automatic contributions,

521
00:16:30,885 --> 00:16:32,174
same raise rule,

522
00:16:32,174 --> 00:16:33,785
same low cost funds.

523
00:16:33,965 --> 00:16:35,150
If you get a bonus,

524
00:16:35,150 --> 00:16:37,332
put a large share toward investing.

525
00:16:37,512 --> 00:16:39,970
And when you cross one hundred thousand,

526
00:16:39,970 --> 00:16:43,535
celebrate modestly, then raise your automatic contribution

527
00:16:43,535 --> 00:16:44,272
by a little,

528
00:16:44,272 --> 00:16:45,686
instead of lowering it.

529
00:16:46,036 --> 00:16:47,835
Why raise it at the finish line?

530
00:16:48,015 --> 00:16:50,581
Because the next one hundred thousand comes

531
00:16:50,581 --> 00:16:51,893
faster than the first,

532
00:16:51,893 --> 00:16:53,922
and the habits you keep now decide

533
00:16:53,922 --> 00:16:54,459
how fast.

534
00:16:54,639 --> 00:16:56,740
One hundred thousand isn't the end of

535
00:16:56,740 --> 00:16:57,251
the road.

536
00:16:57,431 --> 00:16:59,264
It's the point where the road starts

537
00:16:59,264 --> 00:17:00,740
going downhill in your favor.

538
00:17:01,090 --> 00:17:03,719
The second one hundred thousand usually comes

539
00:17:03,719 --> 00:17:05,297
much faster than the first,

540
00:17:05,297 --> 00:17:07,401
because your money is now doing part

541
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:08,102
of the work.

542
00:17:08,282 --> 00:17:10,469
At five hundred dollars a month and

543
00:17:10,469 --> 00:17:13,156
seven percent, roughly eleven years for the

544
00:17:13,156 --> 00:17:15,281
first, and only about six more for

545
00:17:15,281 --> 00:17:15,968
the second.

546
00:17:16,318 --> 00:17:18,624
A quick guide to where money usually

547
00:17:18,624 --> 00:17:20,033
belongs at each stage.

548
00:17:20,213 --> 00:17:23,322
Your starter cushion and emergency fund belong

549
00:17:23,322 --> 00:17:25,349
in safe, easy to reach places,

550
00:17:25,349 --> 00:17:27,985
like an FDIC insured high yield savings

551
00:17:27,985 --> 00:17:28,526
account.

552
00:17:28,706 --> 00:17:29,569
Not in stocks,

553
00:17:29,569 --> 00:17:31,665
because you might need it during a

554
00:17:31,665 --> 00:17:34,255
market drop, exactly when stocks are down.

555
00:17:34,605 --> 00:17:37,300
Money for goals within a few years,

556
00:17:37,300 --> 00:17:39,533
like a down payment or a car,

557
00:17:39,533 --> 00:17:42,459
also usually belongs somewhere stable,

558
00:17:42,459 --> 00:17:44,153
like savings accounts,

559
00:17:44,153 --> 00:17:46,001
certificates of deposit,

560
00:17:46,001 --> 00:17:47,387
or Treasury bills.

561
00:17:47,567 --> 00:17:50,025
Money for retirement and goals ten or

562
00:17:50,025 --> 00:17:52,814
more years away is where diversified stock

563
00:17:52,814 --> 00:17:54,940
investments make the most sense,

564
00:17:54,940 --> 00:17:57,796
because there's time to recover from drops.

565
00:17:58,146 --> 00:18:00,890
And the order of accounts many people

566
00:18:00,890 --> 00:18:03,413
follow is: employer plan up to the

567
00:18:03,413 --> 00:18:04,822
match, then an IRA,

568
00:18:04,822 --> 00:18:07,122
then more in the employer plan,

569
00:18:07,122 --> 00:18:09,570
then a regular brokerage account.

570
00:18:09,750 --> 00:18:12,066
If you're eligible for a health savings

571
00:18:12,066 --> 00:18:14,382
account, it can be a powerful addition.

572
00:18:14,562 --> 00:18:17,230
The right order depends on your situation,

573
00:18:17,230 --> 00:18:19,009
and limits change each year.

574
00:18:19,359 --> 00:18:21,774
The common mistake in stage six is

575
00:18:21,774 --> 00:18:24,757
changing the plan right before the finish.

576
00:18:24,937 --> 00:18:27,090
Some people move everything to cash to

577
00:18:27,090 --> 00:18:28,337
protect the milestone,

578
00:18:28,337 --> 00:18:30,377
then miss the growth that would have

579
00:18:30,377 --> 00:18:31,567
carried them past it.

580
00:18:31,747 --> 00:18:33,812
Others get impatient and take a big

581
00:18:33,812 --> 00:18:35,288
risk to get there faster.

582
00:18:35,468 --> 00:18:37,441
The milestone doesn't need protecting.

583
00:18:37,621 --> 00:18:38,759
The habit does.

584
00:18:39,109 --> 00:18:40,200
Want to speed it up?

585
00:18:40,380 --> 00:18:42,261
Here are five accelerators.

586
00:18:42,441 --> 00:18:43,788
Accelerator one.

587
00:18:43,968 --> 00:18:45,384
Raise your income early.

588
00:18:45,564 --> 00:18:47,911
A higher income in your twenties or

589
00:18:47,911 --> 00:18:50,324
early thirties has the most years to

590
00:18:50,324 --> 00:18:50,928
compound.

591
00:18:51,108 --> 00:18:52,373
Accelerator two.

592
00:18:52,553 --> 00:18:54,078
Cut one big expense,

593
00:18:54,078 --> 00:18:55,755
like housing or a car,

594
00:18:55,755 --> 00:18:57,813
instead of many small ones.

595
00:18:57,993 --> 00:18:59,887
One big win can free up hundreds

596
00:18:59,887 --> 00:19:01,011
of dollars a month.

597
00:19:01,361 --> 00:19:02,719
Accelerator three.

598
00:19:02,899 --> 00:19:05,629
Capture every dollar of employer match,

599
00:19:05,629 --> 00:19:07,868
and use tax advantaged accounts.

600
00:19:08,048 --> 00:19:09,290
Accelerator four.

601
00:19:09,470 --> 00:19:11,339
Live on one income if you're a

602
00:19:11,339 --> 00:19:12,648
two income household,

603
00:19:12,648 --> 00:19:14,455
and invest most of the other,

604
00:19:14,455 --> 00:19:15,763
even for a few years.

605
00:19:15,943 --> 00:19:17,371
And accelerator five.

606
00:19:17,551 --> 00:19:21,063
Send windfalls, like bonuses and refunds,

607
00:19:21,063 --> 00:19:22,776
mostly to investing.

608
00:19:23,126 --> 00:19:25,356
Five hundred dollars a month sounds like

609
00:19:25,356 --> 00:19:26,527
a lot to many people.

610
00:19:26,707 --> 00:19:27,897
So let's find it,

611
00:19:27,897 --> 00:19:29,436
on an ordinary budget.

612
00:19:29,786 --> 00:19:31,687
Start with the big three:

613
00:19:31,687 --> 00:19:34,197
housing, transportation and food.

614
00:19:34,377 --> 00:19:36,861
Moving to a slightly cheaper apartment at

615
00:19:36,861 --> 00:19:39,042
renewal, or getting a roommate for a

616
00:19:39,042 --> 00:19:41,343
while, might free two hundred dollars.

617
00:19:41,523 --> 00:19:44,394
Keeping your current car instead of upgrading,

618
00:19:44,394 --> 00:19:46,703
or refinancing an expensive car loan,

619
00:19:46,703 --> 00:19:48,513
might free one hundred fifty.

620
00:19:48,863 --> 00:19:50,244
Then the smaller leaks.

621
00:19:50,424 --> 00:19:52,321
Cancel unused subscriptions,

622
00:19:52,321 --> 00:19:53,675
maybe forty dollars.

623
00:19:53,855 --> 00:19:55,975
Cook a few more dinners at home

624
00:19:55,975 --> 00:19:58,162
each week, maybe eighty dollars.

625
00:19:58,342 --> 00:20:00,726
Shop your phone plan and insurance,

626
00:20:00,726 --> 00:20:01,883
maybe forty more.

627
00:20:02,063 --> 00:20:02,616
Add it up,

628
00:20:02,616 --> 00:20:04,218
and you're near five hundred,

629
00:20:04,218 --> 00:20:06,429
without changing your life dramatically.

630
00:20:06,779 --> 00:20:08,729
And if the budget truly has no

631
00:20:08,729 --> 00:20:10,875
slack, the money has to come from

632
00:20:10,875 --> 00:20:11,330
income.

633
00:20:11,510 --> 00:20:13,960
A raise, a better paying job,

634
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:16,664
overtime, or a side income for a

635
00:20:16,664 --> 00:20:17,593
set period.

636
00:20:17,773 --> 00:20:19,789
Many people use a combination:

637
00:20:19,789 --> 00:20:20,863
cut two hundred,

638
00:20:20,863 --> 00:20:22,475
earn three hundred more.

639
00:20:22,655 --> 00:20:25,023
Five hundred dollars a month isn't one

640
00:20:25,023 --> 00:20:25,895
big sacrifice.

641
00:20:26,075 --> 00:20:29,244
It's usually five or six small decisions.

642
00:20:29,594 --> 00:20:31,869
Let's see the plan at three incomes.

643
00:20:32,049 --> 00:20:34,197
At forty thousand dollars a year,

644
00:20:34,197 --> 00:20:36,996
investing two hundred fifty dollars a month

645
00:20:36,996 --> 00:20:39,144
is about seven and a half percent

646
00:20:39,144 --> 00:20:39,990
of gross pay.

647
00:20:40,170 --> 00:20:42,794
Adding a three percent employer match helps.

648
00:20:42,974 --> 00:20:45,427
The journey might take fifteen years or

649
00:20:45,427 --> 00:20:47,754
more, but income growth along the way

650
00:20:47,754 --> 00:20:49,012
usually shortens it.

651
00:20:49,362 --> 00:20:50,603
At sixty thousand,

652
00:20:50,603 --> 00:20:53,016
five hundred a month is ten percent

653
00:20:53,016 --> 00:20:53,913
of gross pay.

654
00:20:54,093 --> 00:20:54,977
With a match,

655
00:20:54,977 --> 00:20:56,542
maybe thirteen percent.

656
00:20:56,722 --> 00:20:58,492
That's the eleven year path,

657
00:20:58,492 --> 00:21:00,136
often shorter with raises.

658
00:21:00,316 --> 00:21:02,174
And at one hundred thousand,

659
00:21:02,174 --> 00:21:04,697
one thousand a month is twelve percent

660
00:21:04,697 --> 00:21:05,559
of gross pay,

661
00:21:05,559 --> 00:21:07,351
about six and a half years.

662
00:21:07,531 --> 00:21:09,617
Higher incomes make it faster,

663
00:21:09,617 --> 00:21:12,188
but only if lifestyle doesn't rise to

664
00:21:12,188 --> 00:21:12,605
match.

665
00:21:12,955 --> 00:21:15,114
Notice the percentages are similar.

666
00:21:15,294 --> 00:21:17,570
Around ten to fifteen percent.

667
00:21:17,750 --> 00:21:19,619
The plan scales with your income.

668
00:21:19,799 --> 00:21:21,575
What doesn't scale is the habit.

669
00:21:21,755 --> 00:21:23,406
That has to be built at whatever

670
00:21:23,406 --> 00:21:24,542
income you have today.

671
00:21:24,892 --> 00:21:26,075
Before the stories,

672
00:21:26,075 --> 00:21:28,254
four mistakes that can add years to

673
00:21:28,254 --> 00:21:29,002
the journey.

674
00:21:29,182 --> 00:21:30,076
Mistake one.

675
00:21:30,256 --> 00:21:33,188
Cashing out a retirement account when changing

676
00:21:33,188 --> 00:21:33,506
jobs.

677
00:21:33,686 --> 00:21:35,484
Taxes, possible penalties,

678
00:21:35,484 --> 00:21:38,043
and lost compounding can set you back

679
00:21:38,043 --> 00:21:38,458
years.

680
00:21:38,638 --> 00:21:40,066
Roll it over instead.

681
00:21:40,246 --> 00:21:41,268
Mistake two.

682
00:21:41,448 --> 00:21:43,876
Taking a big loan for a depreciating

683
00:21:43,876 --> 00:21:45,831
asset, like an expensive car,

684
00:21:45,831 --> 00:21:47,787
in the middle of the journey.

685
00:21:48,137 --> 00:21:49,158
Mistake three.

686
00:21:49,338 --> 00:21:51,936
Chasing hot investments with a large share

687
00:21:51,936 --> 00:21:52,926
of your savings.

688
00:21:53,106 --> 00:21:55,139
One big loss can erase years of

689
00:21:55,139 --> 00:21:55,730
progress.

690
00:21:55,910 --> 00:21:57,106
And mistake four.

691
00:21:57,286 --> 00:22:00,503
Stopping contributions for a long period during

692
00:22:00,503 --> 00:22:01,256
a downturn.

693
00:22:01,436 --> 00:22:03,476
Early dollars have the most time to

694
00:22:03,476 --> 00:22:06,332
grow, and dollars invested during downturns often

695
00:22:06,332 --> 00:22:07,148
grow the most.

696
00:22:07,328 --> 00:22:08,330
If you need to,

697
00:22:08,330 --> 00:22:11,136
reduce contributions, but try not to stop.

698
00:22:11,487 --> 00:22:13,294
Here's a simple tool that makes the

699
00:22:13,294 --> 00:22:14,378
whole journey easier.

700
00:22:14,558 --> 00:22:15,974
A one page tracker.

701
00:22:16,154 --> 00:22:17,764
You can do it in a notebook

702
00:22:17,764 --> 00:22:18,778
or a spreadsheet.

703
00:22:19,128 --> 00:22:19,776
At the top,

704
00:22:19,776 --> 00:22:20,718
write your goal,

705
00:22:20,718 --> 00:22:22,427
one hundred thousand dollars,

706
00:22:22,427 --> 00:22:23,899
and the date you started.

707
00:22:24,079 --> 00:22:26,111
Below it, draw six boxes,

708
00:22:26,111 --> 00:22:27,655
one for each stage.

709
00:22:27,835 --> 00:22:29,629
Each time you finish a stage,

710
00:22:29,629 --> 00:22:31,237
write the date in the box.

711
00:22:31,417 --> 00:22:33,275
It sounds almost childish.

712
00:22:33,455 --> 00:22:35,261
But seeing the boxes fill up over

713
00:22:35,261 --> 00:22:37,286
the years is surprisingly motivating.

714
00:22:37,636 --> 00:22:38,763
Under the boxes,

715
00:22:38,763 --> 00:22:41,442
keep four numbers that you update once

716
00:22:41,442 --> 00:22:43,486
a month: your total invested,

717
00:22:43,486 --> 00:22:44,895
your emergency fund,

718
00:22:44,895 --> 00:22:46,023
your total debt,

719
00:22:46,023 --> 00:22:47,574
and your savings rate.

720
00:22:47,754 --> 00:22:48,625
Once a year,

721
00:22:48,625 --> 00:22:49,568
add one more:

722
00:22:49,568 --> 00:22:50,656
your net worth.

723
00:22:50,836 --> 00:22:52,183
That's the whole tracker.

724
00:22:52,363 --> 00:22:53,605
Five minutes a month.

725
00:22:53,956 --> 00:22:55,082
Why does this help?

726
00:22:55,262 --> 00:22:57,060
Because progress you can see keeps you

727
00:22:57,060 --> 00:22:58,431
going during the long middle.

728
00:22:58,611 --> 00:23:01,906
And because writing numbers down regularly catches

729
00:23:01,906 --> 00:23:04,541
problems early, like a savings rate that

730
00:23:04,541 --> 00:23:06,715
slipped, or debt that crept back.

731
00:23:06,895 --> 00:23:08,942
What gets measured gets managed,

732
00:23:08,942 --> 00:23:10,158
as the saying goes.

733
00:23:10,508 --> 00:23:12,122
What if your income isn't steady?

734
00:23:12,302 --> 00:23:13,982
Freelancers, gig workers,

735
00:23:13,982 --> 00:23:17,073
people on commission and seasonal workers face

736
00:23:17,073 --> 00:23:19,291
a harder version of this journey.

737
00:23:19,471 --> 00:23:20,927
The plan still works,

738
00:23:20,927 --> 00:23:22,106
with two changes.

739
00:23:22,286 --> 00:23:24,787
First, a bigger emergency fund,

740
00:23:24,787 --> 00:23:26,803
often six months or more,

741
00:23:26,803 --> 00:23:30,030
because income can drop without warning.

742
00:23:30,380 --> 00:23:32,177
Second, save a percentage,

743
00:23:32,177 --> 00:23:33,491
not a fixed amount.

744
00:23:33,671 --> 00:23:35,589
Every time money comes in,

745
00:23:35,589 --> 00:23:36,843
move a set share,

746
00:23:36,843 --> 00:23:38,318
say fifteen percent,

747
00:23:38,318 --> 00:23:40,974
to savings and investing right away.

748
00:23:41,154 --> 00:23:42,205
In good months,

749
00:23:42,205 --> 00:23:43,186
you save more.

750
00:23:43,366 --> 00:23:44,654
In slow months,

751
00:23:44,654 --> 00:23:45,084
less.

752
00:23:45,264 --> 00:23:47,030
And set aside money for taxes if

753
00:23:47,030 --> 00:23:48,190
they're not withheld.

754
00:23:48,370 --> 00:23:51,029
Many freelancers keep a separate account just

755
00:23:51,029 --> 00:23:51,620
for taxes.

756
00:23:51,971 --> 00:23:54,687
Some people with irregular income also pay

757
00:23:54,687 --> 00:23:57,340
themselves a steady salary from a holding

758
00:23:57,340 --> 00:23:57,857
account.

759
00:23:58,037 --> 00:24:00,056
All income goes into one account,

760
00:24:00,056 --> 00:24:02,259
and a fixed amount moves to checking

761
00:24:02,259 --> 00:24:03,238
every two weeks.

762
00:24:03,418 --> 00:24:05,489
It turns a bumpy income into a

763
00:24:05,489 --> 00:24:08,249
smooth one, which makes every other part

764
00:24:08,249 --> 00:24:09,560
of the plan easier.

765
00:24:09,910 --> 00:24:11,276
If you're in a couple,

766
00:24:11,276 --> 00:24:13,201
the journey can go much faster,

767
00:24:13,201 --> 00:24:14,133
or much slower,

768
00:24:14,133 --> 00:24:16,307
depending on how you work together.

769
00:24:16,487 --> 00:24:19,910
Start with one honest conversation about goals,

770
00:24:19,910 --> 00:24:21,293
debts and spending.

771
00:24:21,473 --> 00:24:23,598
Many couples avoid it for years,

772
00:24:23,598 --> 00:24:24,527
and lose time.

773
00:24:24,877 --> 00:24:26,328
Then decide on a system.

774
00:24:26,508 --> 00:24:28,540
Some couples combine everything.

775
00:24:28,720 --> 00:24:31,071
Some keep separate accounts and share a

776
00:24:31,071 --> 00:24:33,120
joint account for bills and goals.

777
00:24:33,300 --> 00:24:34,217
Both can work.

778
00:24:34,397 --> 00:24:36,578
What matters is a shared target,

779
00:24:36,578 --> 00:24:38,692
shared automatic contributions,

780
00:24:38,692 --> 00:24:41,282
and a monthly fifteen minute check in.

781
00:24:41,462 --> 00:24:43,517
Celebrate each stage together.

782
00:24:43,867 --> 00:24:44,703
One more tip.

783
00:24:44,883 --> 00:24:46,622
If one partner earns more,

784
00:24:46,622 --> 00:24:49,565
contributions can be proportional to income,

785
00:24:49,565 --> 00:24:50,769
rather than equal.

786
00:24:50,949 --> 00:24:52,507
That keeps things fair,

787
00:24:52,507 --> 00:24:53,997
and avoids resentment,

788
00:24:53,997 --> 00:24:56,369
which can derail a plan faster than

789
00:24:56,369 --> 00:24:57,520
any market crash.

790
00:24:57,870 --> 00:24:59,298
One more honest point.

791
00:24:59,478 --> 00:25:00,729
Because of inflation,

792
00:25:00,729 --> 00:25:03,290
one hundred thousand dollars ten years from

793
00:25:03,290 --> 00:25:05,076
now will buy less than it does

794
00:25:05,076 --> 00:25:05,434
today.

795
00:25:05,614 --> 00:25:07,291
At three percent inflation,

796
00:25:07,291 --> 00:25:09,651
it would buy roughly what seventy four

797
00:25:09,651 --> 00:25:10,769
thousand buys now.

798
00:25:10,949 --> 00:25:12,902
So the milestone is a little less

799
00:25:12,902 --> 00:25:15,032
impressive in real terms by the time

800
00:25:15,032 --> 00:25:15,802
you reach it.

801
00:25:16,152 --> 00:25:18,898
But that's another reason to invest rather

802
00:25:18,898 --> 00:25:19,879
than just save.

803
00:25:20,059 --> 00:25:23,762
Investments have historically grown faster than inflation

804
00:25:23,762 --> 00:25:24,931
over long periods,

805
00:25:24,931 --> 00:25:26,490
while cash often hasn't.

806
00:25:26,670 --> 00:25:28,638
And it's a reason to raise your

807
00:25:28,638 --> 00:25:30,161
contributions over time,

808
00:25:30,161 --> 00:25:32,255
roughly in line with your income.

809
00:25:32,435 --> 00:25:34,710
That keeps your plan growing in real

810
00:25:34,710 --> 00:25:36,289
terms, not just on paper.

811
00:25:36,640 --> 00:25:38,126
Let's look at three paths.

812
00:25:38,306 --> 00:25:39,865
Jordan, twenty six,

813
00:25:39,865 --> 00:25:41,917
a junior software tester.

814
00:25:42,097 --> 00:25:43,078
Starts at zero,

815
00:25:43,078 --> 00:25:45,501
invests four hundred dollars a month,

816
00:25:45,501 --> 00:25:47,530
and raises it with every raise.

817
00:25:47,710 --> 00:25:48,873
After five years,

818
00:25:48,873 --> 00:25:51,472
he's investing twelve hundred a month.

819
00:25:51,652 --> 00:25:54,033
He reaches one hundred thousand in about

820
00:25:54,033 --> 00:25:55,402
seven and a half years.

821
00:25:55,582 --> 00:25:57,973
His accelerator was income growth.

822
00:25:58,323 --> 00:25:59,814
Teresa, thirty three,

823
00:25:59,814 --> 00:26:02,654
a nurse with sixteen thousand dollars of

824
00:26:02,654 --> 00:26:04,430
credit card and car debt.

825
00:26:04,610 --> 00:26:06,528
She spends her first two and a

826
00:26:06,528 --> 00:26:08,639
half years in stages one and two,

827
00:26:08,639 --> 00:26:11,518
clearing debt and building an emergency fund.

828
00:26:11,698 --> 00:26:13,920
Then she redirects those payments,

829
00:26:13,920 --> 00:26:16,208
about one thousand dollars a month,

830
00:26:16,208 --> 00:26:17,189
into investing.

831
00:26:17,369 --> 00:26:20,078
She reaches one hundred thousand around nine

832
00:26:20,078 --> 00:26:22,048
and a half years after starting.

833
00:26:22,228 --> 00:26:24,701
Her accelerator was the rolled debt payment.

834
00:26:25,051 --> 00:26:26,254
And Sam and Priya,

835
00:26:26,254 --> 00:26:28,059
a couple in their thirties,

836
00:26:28,059 --> 00:26:30,867
each earning about sixty thousand dollars.

837
00:26:31,047 --> 00:26:32,968
They decide to live on one income

838
00:26:32,968 --> 00:26:34,889
for four years and invest most of

839
00:26:34,889 --> 00:26:35,471
the other.

840
00:26:35,651 --> 00:26:38,526
Investing about two thousand five hundred dollars

841
00:26:38,526 --> 00:26:40,873
a month, they reach one hundred thousand

842
00:26:40,873 --> 00:26:42,105
in about three years,

843
00:26:42,105 --> 00:26:44,393
then relax their savings rate a little.

844
00:26:44,573 --> 00:26:47,032
Their accelerator was a high savings rate

845
00:26:47,032 --> 00:26:48,172
for a short period.

846
00:26:48,522 --> 00:26:50,368
Three very different paths.

847
00:26:50,548 --> 00:26:52,134
One focused on income,

848
00:26:52,134 --> 00:26:53,432
one on debt first,

849
00:26:53,432 --> 00:26:55,668
one on an intense savings rate.

850
00:26:55,848 --> 00:26:57,701
All three used automation,

851
00:26:57,701 --> 00:26:59,696
avoided big new fixed costs,

852
00:26:59,696 --> 00:27:02,547
and kept investing through market drops.

853
00:27:02,727 --> 00:27:03,853
The details differ.

854
00:27:04,033 --> 00:27:05,868
The stages and the habits are the

855
00:27:05,868 --> 00:27:06,146
same.

856
00:27:06,496 --> 00:27:08,818
People who reach their first one hundred

857
00:27:08,818 --> 00:27:10,791
thousand often say the same thing.

858
00:27:10,971 --> 00:27:12,597
It didn't feel like a big moment.

859
00:27:12,777 --> 00:27:14,286
There was no fireworks day.

860
00:27:14,466 --> 00:27:17,075
The balance just quietly crossed a line

861
00:27:17,075 --> 00:27:18,414
on a random Tuesday.

862
00:27:18,594 --> 00:27:19,905
What changed wasn't the day.

863
00:27:20,085 --> 00:27:21,653
It was everything around it.

864
00:27:22,003 --> 00:27:24,383
Money stopped feeling like an emergency.

865
00:27:24,563 --> 00:27:27,628
A surprise bill became a minor annoyance.

866
00:27:27,808 --> 00:27:31,244
Job decisions became choices instead of necessities.

867
00:27:31,424 --> 00:27:32,233
And for many,

868
00:27:32,233 --> 00:27:34,222
the biggest change was internal.

869
00:27:34,402 --> 00:27:36,249
They had proof that they could set

870
00:27:36,249 --> 00:27:37,607
a long goal and reach it.

871
00:27:37,787 --> 00:27:40,132
That proof makes every next goal easier.

872
00:27:40,482 --> 00:27:42,397
And many say the same regret.

873
00:27:42,577 --> 00:27:44,180
I wish I'd started sooner,

874
00:27:44,180 --> 00:27:45,782
even with smaller amounts.

875
00:27:45,962 --> 00:27:47,839
If you're at the very beginning right

876
00:27:47,839 --> 00:27:49,260
now, this is the part of the

877
00:27:49,260 --> 00:27:50,072
story you're in.

878
00:27:50,252 --> 00:27:52,747
It's the part everyone wishes they'd started

879
00:27:52,747 --> 00:27:53,201
earlier.

880
00:27:53,551 --> 00:27:55,641
Notice also what none of them did.

881
00:27:55,821 --> 00:27:57,992
None of them found a secret investment.

882
00:27:58,172 --> 00:27:59,867
None of them timed the market.

883
00:28:00,047 --> 00:28:01,962
None of them earned a huge salary

884
00:28:01,962 --> 00:28:02,717
at the start.

885
00:28:02,897 --> 00:28:04,990
They followed the stages in order,

886
00:28:04,990 --> 00:28:07,083
adjusted when life got in the way,

887
00:28:07,083 --> 00:28:09,607
and kept the automatic transfers running.

888
00:28:09,787 --> 00:28:11,295
That's the whole secret,

889
00:28:11,295 --> 00:28:13,809
and it's available to almost anyone with

890
00:28:13,809 --> 00:28:16,196
a steady income and a little patience.

891
00:28:16,546 --> 00:28:18,081
And each of them says the same

892
00:28:18,081 --> 00:28:20,076
thing about the moment they crossed one

893
00:28:20,076 --> 00:28:20,946
hundred thousand.

894
00:28:21,126 --> 00:28:23,401
It wasn't the money that felt best.

895
00:28:23,581 --> 00:28:25,164
It was knowing the hardest part was

896
00:28:25,164 --> 00:28:25,706
behind them.

897
00:28:26,056 --> 00:28:28,133
Let me answer the questions people ask

898
00:28:28,133 --> 00:28:30,045
me most about the first one hundred

899
00:28:30,045 --> 00:28:30,537
thousand.

900
00:28:30,887 --> 00:28:31,781
Question one.

901
00:28:31,961 --> 00:28:33,249
Does home equity count?

902
00:28:33,429 --> 00:28:34,685
For net worth,

903
00:28:34,685 --> 00:28:35,043
yes.

904
00:28:35,223 --> 00:28:36,303
But in this plan,

905
00:28:36,303 --> 00:28:38,718
I focus on invested money and savings,

906
00:28:38,718 --> 00:28:41,577
because home equity doesn't compound the same

907
00:28:41,577 --> 00:28:43,420
way and can't easily be used.

908
00:28:43,600 --> 00:28:46,259
A paid down mortgage is valuable.

909
00:28:46,439 --> 00:28:48,517
It's just a different kind of progress.

910
00:28:48,867 --> 00:28:49,738
Question two.

911
00:28:49,918 --> 00:28:51,914
Should I pay off student loans first?

912
00:28:52,094 --> 00:28:53,290
It depends on the rate.

913
00:28:53,470 --> 00:28:55,860
High interest loans are often worth paying

914
00:28:55,860 --> 00:28:56,884
down aggressively.

915
00:28:57,064 --> 00:28:59,484
Lower rate loans can usually be paid

916
00:28:59,484 --> 00:29:01,433
on schedule while you invest,

917
00:29:01,433 --> 00:29:04,122
especially to capture an employer match.

918
00:29:04,302 --> 00:29:06,884
Check whether you qualify for any federal

919
00:29:06,884 --> 00:29:08,459
repayment programs first.

920
00:29:08,809 --> 00:29:09,796
Question three.

921
00:29:09,976 --> 00:29:12,181
What if I'm forty and just starting?

922
00:29:12,361 --> 00:29:13,697
You can still get there.

923
00:29:13,877 --> 00:29:16,051
You'll need a higher monthly amount,

924
00:29:16,051 --> 00:29:18,708
which is often possible because income tends

925
00:29:18,708 --> 00:29:20,460
to be higher in your forties.

926
00:29:20,640 --> 00:29:22,648
At one thousand dollars a month,

927
00:29:22,648 --> 00:29:24,594
it takes roughly six and a half

928
00:29:24,594 --> 00:29:26,038
years at seven percent.

929
00:29:26,218 --> 00:29:27,523
And from age fifty,

930
00:29:27,523 --> 00:29:30,270
catch up contributions let you save more

931
00:29:30,270 --> 00:29:31,849
in retirement accounts.

932
00:29:32,199 --> 00:29:33,139
Question four.

933
00:29:33,319 --> 00:29:35,369
Should I pick individual stocks to get

934
00:29:35,369 --> 00:29:36,071
there faster?

935
00:29:36,251 --> 00:29:37,156
It's tempting.

936
00:29:37,336 --> 00:29:39,243
But individual stocks add risk,

937
00:29:39,243 --> 00:29:41,150
and most people who try to beat

938
00:29:41,150 --> 00:29:43,487
the market don't succeed over the long

939
00:29:43,487 --> 00:29:43,733
run.

940
00:29:43,913 --> 00:29:46,239
Many people keep the core of their

941
00:29:46,239 --> 00:29:48,086
money in diversified funds,

942
00:29:48,086 --> 00:29:50,275
and if they want to pick stocks,

943
00:29:50,275 --> 00:29:52,396
use only a small slice they can

944
00:29:52,396 --> 00:29:53,422
afford to lose.

945
00:29:53,772 --> 00:29:54,759
Question five.

946
00:29:54,939 --> 00:29:56,715
Should I use a robo advisor?

947
00:29:56,895 --> 00:29:59,219
Many robo advisors offer simple,

948
00:29:59,219 --> 00:30:03,213
diversified portfolios with automatic rebalancing for a

949
00:30:03,213 --> 00:30:04,012
modest fee.

950
00:30:04,192 --> 00:30:05,470
They can be a good fit if

951
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:07,106
you want things handled for you.

952
00:30:07,286 --> 00:30:09,660
Compare their total cost with a target

953
00:30:09,660 --> 00:30:12,220
date fund, which can do something similar

954
00:30:12,220 --> 00:30:13,532
inside a single fund.

955
00:30:13,882 --> 00:30:15,078
Question six.

956
00:30:15,258 --> 00:30:17,324
How often should I check my progress?

957
00:30:17,504 --> 00:30:19,520
Once a month for contributions,

958
00:30:19,520 --> 00:30:21,340
and once or twice a year for

959
00:30:21,340 --> 00:30:22,380
the big picture.

960
00:30:22,560 --> 00:30:25,473
Checking daily tends to increase anxiety and

961
00:30:25,473 --> 00:30:27,922
the temptation to react to short term

962
00:30:27,922 --> 00:30:28,319
moves.

963
00:30:28,669 --> 00:30:29,749
Question seven.

964
00:30:29,929 --> 00:30:31,031
What about kids?

965
00:30:31,211 --> 00:30:33,057
Should I save for their college first?

966
00:30:33,237 --> 00:30:36,310
Generally, many planners suggest securing your own

967
00:30:36,310 --> 00:30:37,661
retirement path first,

968
00:30:37,661 --> 00:30:39,382
at least the employer match,

969
00:30:39,382 --> 00:30:41,778
because kids can borrow for college but

970
00:30:41,778 --> 00:30:43,744
you can't borrow for retirement.

971
00:30:43,924 --> 00:30:46,074
Once your plan is on track,

972
00:30:46,074 --> 00:30:48,702
a 529 college savings plan can be

973
00:30:48,702 --> 00:30:51,250
a good tool for education goals.

974
00:30:51,601 --> 00:30:52,704
And question eight.

975
00:30:52,884 --> 00:30:55,065
What if the market crashes right before

976
00:30:55,065 --> 00:30:56,576
I hit one hundred thousand?

977
00:30:56,756 --> 00:30:57,615
It might.

978
00:30:57,795 --> 00:31:00,106
Your balance could fall back to eighty,

979
00:31:00,106 --> 00:31:02,300
or even seventy thousand for a while.

980
00:31:02,480 --> 00:31:05,328
That's normal and temporary in most historical

981
00:31:05,328 --> 00:31:07,124
cases, though not guaranteed.

982
00:31:07,304 --> 00:31:08,290
Keep investing.

983
00:31:08,470 --> 00:31:11,146
Many people reach the milestone faster after

984
00:31:11,146 --> 00:31:13,639
a crash, because they bought cheap shares

985
00:31:13,639 --> 00:31:14,612
on the way down.

986
00:31:14,962 --> 00:31:16,918
If you're starting from zero today,

987
00:31:16,918 --> 00:31:18,874
here's your homework for this week.

988
00:31:19,054 --> 00:31:20,958
Open a separate savings account.

989
00:31:21,138 --> 00:31:24,025
Set up an automatic transfer for payday,

990
00:31:24,025 --> 00:31:24,819
any amount.

991
00:31:24,999 --> 00:31:27,137
And write the six stage boxes on

992
00:31:27,137 --> 00:31:28,273
a piece of paper.

993
00:31:28,453 --> 00:31:29,811
That's stage one,

994
00:31:29,811 --> 00:31:30,450
started.

995
00:31:30,630 --> 00:31:32,549
The rest of the journey is just

996
00:31:32,549 --> 00:31:34,159
repeating that first week,

997
00:31:34,159 --> 00:31:35,955
with slightly bigger numbers,

998
00:31:35,955 --> 00:31:36,946
for a few years.

999
00:31:37,296 --> 00:31:38,039
Quick recap.

1000
00:31:38,219 --> 00:31:40,697
The numbers: at five hundred dollars a

1001
00:31:40,697 --> 00:31:42,262
month and seven percent,

1002
00:31:42,262 --> 00:31:43,501
about eleven years.

1003
00:31:43,681 --> 00:31:44,786
At one thousand,

1004
00:31:44,786 --> 00:31:46,236
about six and a half.

1005
00:31:46,416 --> 00:31:48,753
The second half always goes faster than

1006
00:31:48,753 --> 00:31:49,353
the first.

1007
00:31:49,533 --> 00:31:50,688
The six stages:

1008
00:31:50,688 --> 00:31:52,305
zero to one thousand,

1009
00:31:52,305 --> 00:31:53,153
one to ten,

1010
00:31:53,153 --> 00:31:54,616
ten to twenty five,

1011
00:31:54,616 --> 00:31:56,233
twenty five to fifty,

1012
00:31:56,233 --> 00:31:57,927
fifty to seventy five,

1013
00:31:57,927 --> 00:32:01,085
and seventy five to one hundred thousand.

1014
00:32:01,435 --> 00:32:03,686
The traps: it feels pointless,

1015
00:32:03,686 --> 00:32:06,087
debt fatigue, fear of investing,

1016
00:32:06,087 --> 00:32:07,437
the boring middle,

1017
00:32:07,437 --> 00:32:10,514
bigger drops and the finish line feeling.

1018
00:32:10,694 --> 00:32:11,996
And the playbook:

1019
00:32:11,996 --> 00:32:13,374
a starter cushion,

1020
00:32:13,374 --> 00:32:14,830
the match and debt,

1021
00:32:14,830 --> 00:32:17,051
start investing, grow income,

1022
00:32:17,051 --> 00:32:19,119
paperwork and tax accounts,

1023
00:32:19,119 --> 00:32:20,574
and the final push.

1024
00:32:20,754 --> 00:32:22,066
Keep the system running,

1025
00:32:22,066 --> 00:32:23,761
and let the road tilt your way.

1026
00:32:24,111 --> 00:32:25,855
If you want this plan in more

1027
00:32:25,855 --> 00:32:28,260
detail, with worksheets for every stage,

1028
00:32:28,260 --> 00:32:29,463
it's in my playbook.

1029
00:32:29,643 --> 00:32:31,257
The link is in the description.

1030
00:32:31,437 --> 00:32:33,520
And watch my video on what changes

1031
00:32:33,520 --> 00:32:36,092
when you hit one hundred thousand dollars.

1032
00:32:36,272 --> 00:32:38,094
It's the reward at the end of

1033
00:32:38,094 --> 00:32:38,722
this road.

1034
00:32:38,902 --> 00:32:40,098
I'm Ryan Rover.

1035
00:32:40,278 --> 00:32:41,532
See you in the next one.
